  "|Based on the prescribed poems: \nIn Robert Frost's 'Wild Grapes' the girl's brother throws down grapes in the manner he does to|make his sister have her fill|allow himself time in-between to eat|make his sister desire to climb the tree|allow himself to have some fun": "set-non-african-poetry",
  "|Based on the prescribed poems: \nDonne's 'Death, be not Proud' is|an epic|a dirge|a ballad|a sonnet": "set-non-african-poetry",
  "|Based on the prescribed poems: \nThe arrangement of David Diop's 'Loser of Everything' in two stanzas reflects his use of|reinforcement|enjambment|contrast|amplification": "set-african-poetry",
  "|Based on the prescribed poems: \n'As if men hung here unblown, Their mildewed buds of love like pollen, Late caught, damp in a swollen...'\nThe sound device in the stanza above from Kalu Uka's 'Earth to Earth' is|onomatopoeia|a refrain|rhyme|repetition": "set-african-poetry",
